100 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (Growing up through elementary and middle school, I learned that I should practice each particular bol 100 times per day if I wanted to perfect it. If I perfected it, I could perform at the next Diwali function in Edison. At that function is going to be Vijaya Aunty whose daughter is an Ivy League-educated physician who will be so impressed at little, cheeky Atishay playing tabla and will potentially give him shadowing opportunities down the line. Shadowing opportunities and clout from Indian aunties?! Performing was a no-brainer for me.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
101 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (With time, I began to genuinely enjoy the taals I was learning. I still remember the day I could finally play tabla alongside my favorite Bollywood song at age 10. Salman Khan's performance in Tere Mast Mast Do Nain was who I aspired to be back then: a ripped, Bollywood-actor who got all the women. How I would get there was almost entirely determined by agreeing to perform in front of random crowds of drunk Indians at an educational gala fundraiser \(most likely a tax-front\), and then for those same Indians the next morning at the mandir.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
